<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE ussf-317 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>RETIMED 2026-11-20 (checked ~2:10 p.m. PST Fri 20 Nov 2026): T0 is 2026-11-21T04:20:00Z (t0_kind window_open; Fri 20 Nov 8:20 p.m. PT), moved from 2026-11-21T02:32:00Z by +6480 s. SpaceX https://www.spacex.com/launches/ussf317: targeting Friday, November 20; the four-hour launch window opens at 8:20 p.m. PT. Backup Saturday, November 21 at 8:12 p.m. PT (2026-11-22T04:12:00Z). No separate window-close instant is published; the four-hour wording is kept and a close is not derived by adding four hours. Booster lands on OCISLY. Timeline unchanged (MECO 2:25, sep 2:28, SES-1 2:35, fairing 2:56, entry burn 6:03-6:27, landing burn 7:59, landing 8:21). SOURCE CONFLICT: LL2 id 76617033-4dc0-4448-b50c-e5b0d5a18539 is Go, NET 2026-11-21T04:20:35Z (second precision; recorded, not used as T0), last_updated 2026-11-20T17:41:31Z, and still lists window_start 2026-11-21T02:32:00Z and window_end 2026-11-21T06:32:00Z. Those leftover bounds are a source note, not T0 and not the window used in this file. utc shifted; ECEF geometry unchanged; sim not re-run. Orbit, azimuth and deploy remain ILLUSTRATIVE.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 USSF-317 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 9.57 s, kick 3.378 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.400, payload 16714 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.5441-0.001324*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: SpaceX Falcon 9 Block 5 (reusable first stage, droneship recovery) — TIMELINE mode (sim/vehicles/falcon9.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Falcon 9 Block 5 masses from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9 Block 5&#x27; spec table; thrust/Isp from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9&#x27; spec table (citing SpaceX).
TIMELINE mode (tuned 2026-10-25): MECO 146 s, stage sep 150 s, SES-1 156 s, fairing 176 s, SECO-1 (final cutoff) from SpaceX&#x27;s sl-15-16 timeline are hard events.
Throttle profile not published: full published thrust throughout; unburned stage-1 residual stands in for entry/landing propellant.
RETIMED 2026-11-20: SpaceX and LL2 now agree. Operator window open is 2026-11-21T02:32:00Z (Fri 20 Nov 6:32 p.m. PT), four-hour window to 2026-11-21T06:32:00Z; backup Sat 21 Nov 8:12 p.m. PT = 2026-11-22T04:12:00Z. Sources checked 2026-11-20T03:35:00Z (7:35 p.m. PST Thu 19 Nov): https://www.spacex.com/launches/ussf317 (&#x27;targeting Friday, November 20 ... four-hour launch window opens at 6:32 p.m. PT&#x27;) and LL2 id 76617033-4dc0-4448-b50c-e5b0d5a18539, status Go, NET 2026-11-21T02:32:00Z, window 02:32-06:32Z, last_updated 2026-11-20T03:26:30Z. The 2026-11-19 LL2/Spaceflight Now 04:32:55Z disagreement is closed. Published timeline moved to MECO 2:25 (145 s), stage sep 2:28 (148 s), SES-1 2:35 (155 s), fairing 2:56 (176 s), entry burn 6:03-6:27, landing burn 7:59, landing 8:21. Those four ascent events are the hard events; the sim was re-fit. Family-telemetry comparison knots stay at the Iridium NEXT-7 sample times (MECO 146 s, SES-1 156 s, fairing 176 s) and are not this flight. Entry and landing are not modelled. SpaceX: 11th flight, Of Course I Still Love You in the Pacific. Azimuth still 153.56 deg. Surrogate utc shifted +79440 s from 2026-11-20T04:28:00Z; its ECEF geometry is unchanged. ILLUSTRATIVE.
RETIMED 2026-11-19: operator (SpaceX) window open is 2026-11-20T04:28:00Z (Thu 19 Nov 8:28 p.m. PT), four-hour window to 08:28:00Z; backup Fri 20 Nov 8:26 p.m. PT = 2026-11-21T04:26:00Z. Sources: https://www.spacex.com/launches/ussf317 and https://content.spacex.com/api/spacex-website/missions/ussf317. SOURCE CONFLICT: LL2 net and Spaceflight Now both give T-0 2026-11-20T04:32:55Z; LL2 window is still 02:46:00Z-06:46:00Z (id 76617033-4dc0-4448-b50c-e5b0d5a18539, status Go, last_updated 2026-11-19T15:08:34Z, https://ll.thespacedevs.com/2.3.0/launches/76617033-4dc0-4448-b50c-e5b0d5a18539/, https://spaceflightnow.com/launch-schedule/). This file uses the operator window open as T0. Timeline re-checked 2026-11-19 and unchanged (Max-Q 1:07, MECO 2:26, sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:58). SpaceX: 11th flight of the booster, landing on the Of Course I Still Love You droneship in the Pacific (not RTLS, not LZ-4). The ascent sim does not model booster recovery; the unburned stage-1 residual stands in for entry/landing propellant. Azimuth still 153.56 deg (ZLA CARF 11/238-26 Area A polygon unchanged). Re-run of the existing config with only t0 changed. ILLUSTRATIVE.
RETIMED 2026-11-18: NET 2026-11-20T02:46:00Z (Thu 19 Nov 6:46 p.m. PST), LL2 window 02:46-06:46Z, status Go, last_updated 2026-11-18T15:15:09Z. ZLA CARF 11/238-26 Area A (2611200246-2611200708) repeats the 11/212-26 polygon, so azimuth 153.56 deg is unchanged. Public files are the previous fit with utc shifted +85560 s. Not re-run.
RETIMED 2026-11-16: NET moved from 2026-11-18T03:14:00Z to 2026-11-19T03:00:00Z (Wed 18 Nov 7:00 p.m. PST). LL2 id 76617033-4dc0-4448-b50c-e5b0d5a18539, status Go, window 2026-11-19T03:00:00Z-07:00:00Z. A new FAA NOTAM window 2026-11-19 03:00-07:43Z is cited via https://space-notices.com/entry/launch-f9-ussf-317 and https://x.com/NotamUpdates/status/2122337617257943183. On that space-notices entry the active Area A notice is ZLA CARF 11/212-26 (same polygon as 11/116-26, expires 2026-11-19T07:22:00Z), so the 153.56 deg azimuth is unchanged. Re-run of the existing config with only t0 changed. ILLUSTRATIVE.
NEW 2026-11-12: SpaceX ussf317 page: &#x27;targeting Saturday, November 14 ... four-hour launch window opens at 7:55 p.m. PT&#x27; (backup Sun Nov 15 7:41 p.m. PT); LL2 NET 2026-11-15T03:55:00Z Go. Booster: 11th flight (B1100 per Next Spaceflight), OCISLY landing. ILLUSTRATIVE.
Published timeline (SpaceX ussf317, checked 2026-11-12): Max-Q 1:07, MECO 2:26, stage sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:58, entry burn 6:06-6:30, landing burn 7:52, landing 8:11. SECO, orbit, deploy NOT published (classified USSF mission).
INFERRED/ASSUMED: SECO-1 time and parking orbit are borrowed from the Starlink Group 15 analog via the USSF-627 config (LL2: drop zones exact fits with Group 15), not USSF-317 sources. Azimuth 153.56 deg from FAA/ZLA CARF NOTAM 11/116-26 Area A (identical to USSF-627&#x27;s polygon). File ends 2 revs after cutoff (deploy unpublished).
Target (see launch config): insertion 177 km, apoapsis 266 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 153.56 deg; payload 16714 kg.
Pad: 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-21T04:20:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (SpaceX publishes no SECO, restart or deploy time for USSF-317 (national-security payload); propagated 2 revs on the inferred (Group-15-analog, borrowed from USSF-627 config) insertion orbit). From insertion T+519.0 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 88.93 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF end T+11191 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 177.19 km, osculating 174.5 x 269.0 km, i 68.288 deg.</description>
<Placemark><name>Pad (ussf-317)</name><Point><coordinates>-120.6110000,34.6320000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
